  "rule": "Explicit V40 adapter and independent-reader integration. Extend V39's existing full bounded actual-reference rate to absent-contact stance as well as swing/landing, requiring validated phase 0..359, explicitly false pre-command presence and bears_support, positive dt and both wave snapshots active. Preserve V39's exact rate outside the added absent-contact stance selection. Keep all position goals, support plans, slew, gains, smooth lift, floor provenance, contact gates, amplitude ramp, BW5R-B prefix, V20 recovery, motor limits, solver, schedule and behavioral criteria. The existing airborne_reference field records absent contact with full provenance and both rate constructions; it is not a scheduled-swing claim. No force-aware or predicted physical improvement claim.",
  "parameter_basis": "No new gain, cap, timer, correction or threshold. V40 extends the existing full actual-reference finite difference only to explicitly absent-contact stance; its motor coefficient remains 1 + existing damping. Native verification on all 400 saved V39 inputs preserves position paths and gate memories, adds 416 stance joint selections, changes 278 velocities and reaches existing speed caps 133 times versus V39's 82. These saved-input command observations do not predict a physical trajectory.",
  "compatibility_scope": "Distinct V40 policy/profile/memory/receipt identities; unchanged explicit-floor v2 request, finite translation-only box-floor source, pre-command native contact semantics and exact independent replay. Reuse the existing optional airborne_reference receipt without interpreting it as scheduled swing. All old policies retain exact output bytes on the saved V39 input population. Older physical records and runtime images remain immutable.",
